From: Z User <z@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Widen scrollbar to 24px and pin thumb at full width

Makes the vertical scrollbar permanently 24px wide with the thumb
always at full width and zero horizontal offset -- no hover-to-expand
animation, no contract-on-defocus snap. The thumb is the full
ScrollBarSize from the start, so the Expanded/Collapsed VSM states
have nothing left to animate on the width axis.

--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/TermControl.xaml
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/TermControl.xaml
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@
             (GH#9218), where we might need this anyways.
         -->
 
-        <x:Double x:Key="ScrollBarSize">16</x:Double>
+        <x:Double x:Key="ScrollBarSize">24</x:Double>
         <x:String x:Key="ScrollBarExpandBeginTime">0</x:String>
 
         <Style x:Key="ForkedScrollbarTemplate"
@@ -619,7 +619,7 @@
                                               Template="{StaticResource RepeatButtonTemplate}" />
                                 <Thumb x:Name="VerticalThumb"
                                        Grid.Row="2"
-                                       Width="{StaticResource ScrollBarVerticalThumbMinWidth}"
+                                       Width="{StaticResource ScrollBarSize}"
                                        MinHeight="{StaticResource ScrollBarVerticalThumbMinHeight}"
                                        contract7Present:CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                                        AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw"
@@ -629,7 +629,7 @@
                                        RenderTransformOrigin="1,0.5"
                                        Template="{StaticResource VerticalThumbTemplate}">
                                     <Thumb.RenderTransform>
-                                        <TranslateTransform x:Name="VerticalThumbTransform" X="{StaticResource ScrollBarThumbOffset}" />
+                                        <TranslateTransform x:Name="VerticalThumbTransform" X="0" />
                                     </Thumb.RenderTransform>
                                 </Thumb>
 

From: Z User <z@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Remove the redundant Settings entry from the system menu

TerminalWindow::Create() raised SystemMenuChangeRequested with
RS_(L"SettingsMenuItem") + Action::Add, which AppHost forwards to
IslandWindow::AddToSystemMenu -> InsertMenuItemW on the Win32 system
menu (the one you get from right-clicking the title bar or clicking
the terminal icon top-left). That entry lands AFTER the default
"Close" item, breaking the Windows convention that Close is always
the last entry in the system menu.

Removing the raise means Settings is never added to the system menu.
Settings stays reachable three other ways: the Ctrl+, key chord,
the command palette, and the new-tab dropdown (TerminalPage.cpp
builds settingsItem independently of this system-menu path).

_OpenSettingsUI was only referenced by the removed raise, so its
definition and declaration are dropped too to avoid MSVC C4505
(unreferenced local function) under /WX.

--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalApp/TerminalWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalApp/TerminalWindow.cpp
@@ -218,10 +218,6 @@
 
         _RefreshThemeRoutine();
 
-        auto args = winrt::make_self<SystemMenuChangeArgs>(RS_(L"SettingsMenuItem"),
-                                                           SystemMenuChangeAction::Add,
-                                                           SystemMenuItemHandler(this, &TerminalWindow::_OpenSettingsUI));
-        SystemMenuChangeRequested.raise(*this, *args);
 
         TraceLoggingWrite(
             g_hTerminalAppProvider,
@@ -789,10 +785,6 @@
         _RefreshThemeRoutine();
     }
 
-    void TerminalWindow::_OpenSettingsUI()
-    {
-        _root->OpenSettingsUI();
-    }
     UIElement TerminalWindow::GetRoot() noexcept
     {
         return _root.as<winrt::Windows::UI::Xaml::Controls::Control>();

--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalApp/TerminalWindow.h
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalApp/TerminalWindow.h
@@ -200,7 +200,6 @@
         void _RefreshThemeRoutine();
         void _OnLoaded(const IInspectable& sender, const Windows::UI::Xaml::RoutedEventArgs& eventArgs);
         void _pageInitialized(const IInspectable& sender, const IInspectable& eventArgs);
-        void _OpenSettingsUI();
         void _WindowSizeChanged(const IInspectable& sender, winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::WindowSizeChangedEventArgs args);
         void _RenameWindowRequested(const IInspectable& sender, const winrt::TerminalApp::RenameWindowRequestedArgs args);
 
